# CrewRig â€” Task06

New asset; old `CrewBody` files, existing FBXs and pivots are unchanged. No Unity, Scripts or Scenes edits.

- Runtime export: `Assets/Art/Models/Crew/CrewRig.fbx`.
- Editable source: `Art/Models/CrewRig/CrewRig.blend`.
- Rebuild: Windows Blender5.2 headless, `Art/Source/build_crew_rig.py`.
- Validate source and FBX: Blender5.2 headless, `Art/Source/validate_crew_rig.py`; results in `validation.json`.
- Contact sheets: Python/Pillow `Art/Source/crew_contact_sheets.py`.
- Previews: `Previews/outfit-turnarounds.png`, `Previews/animation-contact-sheet.png`, 
`Previews/animation-contact-sheet-small.png`; individual rendered frames also retained.

Bare-scalp height **0.95m**, head0.38m (40%); round face, economical eyes/nose/smile, chestnut hair, mitten hands with 
thumbs, thick limbs, rubber boots. Hats extend above scalp. All variants share proportions and rig. Source X right, -Y 
forward, Z up; FBX converts to Unity Y up/+Z facing. Floor pivot is between boots at zero. The armature scale is1; 
source T-pose is the bind pose, previews use authored Idle.

## Mesh selection

Always enable `Body` (skin/face/hair, sleeves, boots/base garment). Enable exactly one skinned garment: 
`Outfit_Captain`, `Outfit_Deckhand`, `Outfit_Fisherman`, `Outfit_Veteran`. Garments include lower coverage and boots 
remain shared. Captain navy jacket has ivory lapels/gold buttons; deckhand yellow bib has straps/pocket; fisherman 
orange oilskins include a hood-down collar; veteran has raised cable-knit ribs and a silver beard.

Hats are separate rigid mesh children of the `HatMount` bone: `Hat_CaptainCap`, `Hat_Beanie`, `Hat_Hood`. Suggested 
combinations Captain/Cap, Deckhand/Beanie, Fisherman/Hood, Veteran/Beanie; enable one hat. Every variant is exported, 
so importing everything visibly stacked is expected until the consumer selects its variant. Source render visibility 
defaults to Deckhand/Beanie.

## Bones

20 total, no leaf/end bones:

```
CrewRig
â”” Hips
  â”œ Spine â†’ Spine1 â†’ Neck â†’ Head â†’ HatMount
  â”‚         â”œ LeftShoulder â†’ LeftArm â†’ LeftForeArm â†’ LeftHand
  â”‚         â”” RightShoulder â†’ RightArm â†’ RightForeArm â†’ RightHand
  â”œ LeftUpLeg â†’ LeftLeg â†’ LeftFoot
  â”” RightUpLeg â†’ RightLeg â†’ RightFoot
```

Shoulder branches attach to Spine1. All five skinned meshes target the same armature, with normalized explicit weights 
and two-bone elbow seam blending. Most chunky pieces use one-bone rigid weights; no finger or facial bones. Hats 
retain a rigid bone relationship. A Unity Generic rig can play these clips directly; Humanoid retargeting/mapping has 
not been tested. Hand bones provide external prop attachment sites. Carry holds an external fish; 
Bait/Cast/Wait/Strike/Reel expect an external rod. Props are deliberately absent from the crew FBX. Row lowers the 
hips 0.15m and folds the legs for a seat; set seat placement in the consumer.

## Actions and timing

24fps, sampled every frame, in place. Duration is (end-start)/24, including identical endpoint keys on loops. No 
horizontal root travel. Set Unity import loop settings explicitly from this table.

| Source action | Frames | Seconds | Loop |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Idle | 1â€“49 | 2 | yes |
| Walk | 1â€“25 | 1 | yes |
| Carry | 1â€“25 | 1 | yes |
| Bait | 1â€“49 | 2 | yes |
| Cast | 1â€“33 | 1.333333 | no |
| Wait | 1â€“49 | 2 | yes |
| Strike | 1â€“19 | 0.75 | no |
| Reel | 1â€“25 | 1 | yes |
| Row | 1â€“49 | 2 | yes |
| Cheer | 1â€“49 | 2 | no |
| Stow | 1â€“49 | 2 | no |

FBX take names include the armature prefix `CrewRig|<Action>`. Blender reimport prefixes once more 
(`CrewRig|CrewRig|<Action>`). Match the suffix after the last `|`, or use the full imported clip name discovered by 
the consumer. Do not assume exact bare action names from an arbitrary FBX importer. Paths are below armature 
`CrewRig`, e.g. `CrewRig/Hips/Spine/Spine1/LeftShoulder/LeftArm`; meshes are siblings of Hips beneath the armature 
root. Integration may introduce another model root.

## Materials

New canonical sRGB: `M_HairChestnut` `#50392E`, `M_HairSilver` `#ADB6AF`. Add these to the game's material remap. All 
other exported materials reuse `M_Skin`, `M_HullNavy`, `M_RailIvory`, `M_OilskinYellow`, `M_SafetyOrange`, `M_Rubber`, 
`M_Steel`. Preview lighting/ground/materials are excluded from FBX. No bitmap textures or Unity material files.

## Validation and limits

Automated source checks: exact bone/mesh/action names;0.95m floor-to-scalp bounds; every skin vertex weighted with 
sum1; all garments use the same armature; rigid hats parented to HatMount;24fps; exact action frame ranges; meaningful 
movement; matching looping endpoint bone matrices. FBX reimport checks: one20-bone armature; all8 expected meshes; 
all11 actions with frame ranges preserved; all20 bones keyed, all imported curves retain one sample per frame and 
durations match the table; metre scale; normalized weights and skin armature relationships. `validation.json` records 
the actual imported names.

Outfit turnaround and animation renders were inspected from front/back/sides and the orthographic game camera. Contact 
sheet uses three distinct key frames per clip (start, one-third, two-thirds). Small sheet permits gameplay-scale 
review. The animations are intentionally broad, procedural authored first-pass clips; Unity scene lighting, exact 
equipment contact alignment, collision/foot IK, Humanoid mapping and runtime playback remain consumer integration 
checks. Tasks07/08 are not implemented by this batch.
